SECTION 1  ·  READ THESE FIRST
Key Terms
These terms appear throughout Author Check and this guide.
Term
	Definition
	Strength of collaboration
	In a table of co-authors, the number of times the selected researcher is named alongside each co-author on publications in Dimensions.
	Percentile of publication output
	The percentile rank of a researcher in Dimensions in terms of the number of publications compared with their peers. “Peers” are all authors who published in the same ANZSRC Field of Research (the field that covers the most of their publications) and with the same first publication year.
	Flagged publication
	A publication in Dimensions that has been identified as associated with one or more atypical events, such as retraction, withdrawal, or matching a fingerprint in Guillaume Cabanac’s Problematic Paper Screener.
	Network flag
	Researchers with a network flag (“Yes”) are approximately 100 times more likely to have been named as an author of a flagged publication. The methodology is based on Porter & McIntosh (2024), https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-71230-8.
	Eligible publication
	For the self-citation indicator: a review paper, research paper, research chapter or conference paper with a minimum of 9 references.
	Self-citation
	A publication where at least one of its authors is also an author of at least one of its references.
	Retraction taxonomy
	A classification of the reasons given for retractions. Author Check maps the reasons in the Retraction Watch database to it.
	SECTION 2
The Indicators in Detail
Author Check lists several indicators to help detect potential research integrity and paper mill activities. Please keep in mind that these indicators are not “metrics” that can be used for benchmarking, and that none of them can determine misconduct by themself.
